WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.404
Phase 1 is read-only, so it
carries no rollback risk,

2
00:00:03.404 --> 00:00:06.513
but anything it misses
can't be repaired later.

3
00:00:06.513 --> 00:00:12.359
It collects every zone, record, forwarder,
DHCP scope and resolution path, including

4
00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:17.951
the health of the data, because stale
records migrate as faithfully as good ones.

5
00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:20.787
Then each component gets
a target and a method.

6
00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.288
Internal zones move to the new platform.

7
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:27.051
External zones need a registrar
change, so they're high risk.

8
00:00:27.051 --> 00:00:30.837
And locator records stay where
domain controllers can register,

9
00:00:30.837 --> 00:00:33.362
because there's no
Azure-native equivalent.

10
00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:38.510
Phase 2 adds the new resolvers without
moving authority, forwarding both ways,

11
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:43.262
with exactly one authoritative path
per namespace so queries don't loop.

12
00:00:43.262 --> 00:00:47.210
Two errors cause most failures
here, and the slide names both.
